.policy "bandit-b305-cipher-modes" revision 1
.guests off
.description "Avoid the ECB cipher mode; it encrypts identical blocks to identical output and leaks patterns in the data, so use an authenticated mode such as GCM."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Generated from today's JSON by docs/rule-syntax/site/translate.py. Display only: not compiled or run.

#include "python/names.rr"

// B305(n): a finding at node n, from clause `bandit:B305`.
// Each rule below is one way the JSON `rule` can match.
// The JSON `constraints` on F are added to every rule.
.violation B305(at: node) "Replace ECB with an authenticated mode such as GCM; ECB leaks patterns in the data."
    suppress nosec "B305"
B305(n) :- n ~ `$F($$$ARGS)`,
    sym_of(F, "cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.modes.ECB").
